  "_readme": [
    "CANONICAL COPY. server/internal/appcatalog/catalog.json is generated from this file",
    "by server/tools/synccatalog — never hand-edit the server copy.",
    "",
    "BEFORE ENABLING REMOVAL ON A REAL OU: reconcile every `family` below against a",
    "reference image with `Get-AppxPackage -AllUsers | Select PackageFamilyName`.",
    "Publisher hashes and package identities change between Windows releases, and a",
    "family that does not match simply never matches anything (fail-safe, but silently",
    "useless). risk_tier=review means an admin must make a deliberate call: the app is",
    "safely removable, but somebody in the org may actually be using it.",
    "",
    "For kind=startup, `family` is the registry Run VALUE NAME, compared case-insensitively and",
    "EXACTLY unless the item sets \"match\": \"prefix\". Prefix is opt-in because short families",
    "over-match real software: \"Skype\" would catch Skype for Business, \"OneDrive\" would catch",
    "OneDriveSetup. A family that matches nothing is harmless; one that matches too much is not.",
    "It is never the value DATA, which is a file path (a forbidden data class)."
  ],
